# Copy to .env, fill in, and lock it down:
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
# .env is git-ignored and excluded from Docker images. docker compose reads it
# and hands the secrets to containers as files (/run/secrets/...), not as
# environment variables. Never paste these values into chats, issues or logs.
#
# Generate each secret instead of inventing one. Use hex: it's URL-safe, so it
# can't break connection URLs.
#   openssl rand -hex 32

# --- Secrets (all required; containers refuse to start if one is empty) ---

# MariaDB root account. Nothing in the app uses it; it only needs to be strong.
MARIADB_ROOT_PASSWORD=
# Password for the `barista` database user the backend and worker connect as.
MARIADB_PASSWORD=
# Redis password (queue between backend and worker).
REDIS_PASSWORD=
# Signs session cookies. At least 32 characters. Changing it logs everyone out.
JWT_SECRET=
# Used only by the worker.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Settings (not secret) ---

# Your time zone (IANA name), e.g. America/Los_Angeles. Brews record their
# device's UTC offset; this is only for older brews that don't, so their
# roast age uses your local date. Empty = UTC.
#BREW_TIMEZONE=

# The address you open the app at, used for the link in rate-later
# reminders (Settings -> Notifications). Default https://localhost:42069;
# set it to the LAN or public address, with its port, so the link works on
# your phone.
#APP_URL=https://192.168.1.20:42069

# Server admins (Settings -> Server: scheduled database backups) are granted
# on the server, not here, after they've registered:
#   docker compose exec backend npm run admin -- grant you@example.com

# Set to false to close sign-ups, e.g. on a server open to the internet
# (create the accounts first). Existing accounts can still log in.
#ALLOW_REGISTRATION=false

# The time zone the backup hour is in (IANA name). Default UTC. Dumps land
# in ./backups next to this file (docs/api/server.md §10).
#BACKUP_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles

# Set to false to keep database dumps on the server: admins can't download
# them in the app (copy them from ./backups instead).
#BACKUP_DOWNLOADS=false

# Only with docker-compose.release.yml: which published build to run. latest
# (from main), testing, dev, or a fixed one such as sha-7a093cd. That file
# also requires every *_DIR setting below.
#IMAGE_TAG=testing

# --- Where data is kept (README: "Run it on a server") ---
# Defaults: Docker named volumes for the database, Redis and the HTTPS CA,
# and ./photos and ./backups next to this file. Set a path to keep one
# elsewhere, e.g. on a disk that's backed up. Changing one later starts it
# empty: move the data first. Docker creates missing folders, and the app sets
# the owner of its photos and backups folders when it starts.
#DB_DATA_DIR=/srv/barista/db
#REDIS_DATA_DIR=/srv/barista/redis
# The CA devices trust: lose it and each device has to trust a new one.
#CADDY_DATA_DIR=/srv/barista/caddy
#PHOTOS_DIR=/srv/barista/photos
#BACKUPS_DIR=/srv/barista/backups

# Where the app is served, over HTTPS from Caddy's own CA (README: "Install
# it on your phone"). Default 127.0.0.1 (this machine only, at
# https://localhost:42069). Set to 0.0.0.0 to reach it from other devices on your
# network. Anyone on that network can then reach it.
#FRONTEND_BIND=0.0.0.0
# The address other devices open it at: this machine's LAN IP, or a name
# your network resolves. Its certificate is made for this address (and
# localhost). Use the same address in APP_URL.
#APP_HOST=192.168.1.20
# Ports on this machine, if 42069 / 42070 are taken (APP_URL must use the
# same HTTPS port, e.g. https://192.168.1.20:8443). The HTTP port redirects
# to HTTPS and serves the CA root at /ca.crt.
#HTTPS_PORT=42069
#HTTP_PORT=42070

# Model the worker uses for brew analysis. Required; must support Structured
# Outputs (strict JSON schema).
OPENAI_MODEL=
# Model that reads bean labels from photos (docs/api/bean-label.md §4d): it
# must take images. Empty uses OPENAI_MODEL.
#OPENAI_VISION_MODEL=
# Model that looks beans up on the web, when a workspace allows it: it must
# support the web_search tool on the Responses API. Empty uses the above.
#OPENAI_WEB_MODEL=
